2026-07-07 20:16:21,601 | AGENT | TechnicalArchitect Agent answered: Our proposed technical architecture is based on our Atelier platform, a Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) platform that can provide an intelligent assistance tool to support professionals in their daily activities. To meet the client's requirements, we propose the following architecture:

We will design a mobile application and a web interface for the service using API-first principles, with REST and webhook APIs to enable integration with existing systems. Our Atelier platform already has API design capabilities, which can be used to create documented APIs that can be embedded in the client's work environment.

For data storage, we will use our vector store component, which is part of the Atelier platform, to store and manage the client's data. The vector store will be hosted on OuraneCloud, which is SecNumCloud-qualified infrastructure, ensuring the security and sovereignty of the client's data.

To integrate with cabinet vauclair associ_s production tools, we will use our business tool integration capabilities, which include connectors and adapters for accounting-production software, payroll software, document-management systems (GED), and electronic invoicing/dematerialisation environments. Our delivery partner, Ligeo Conseil, can assist with the integration process.

For security measures, we will implement single sign-on (SSO) using SAML or OIDC protocols, and user directories using LDAP or Entra ID, to ensure secure access to the system. We will also ensure that data is encrypted and protected in accordance with GDPR regulations.

To meet the response time requirements, our Atelier platform has a median latency of 1.3 seconds, and a p95 latency below 2.5 seconds for common queries, which should be compatible with daily professional use. Our platform can also scale horizontally to handle seasonal peak loads, ensuring high availability during business hours.

Overall, our proposed technical architecture is designed to meet the client's requirements for a mobile application, web interface, integration with existing systems, data storage, security, and response times, while leveraging our Atelier platform and its components.
